1. **Check back** - Safe, realize equity, but leave money on table if I'm ahead\n2. **Value bet (100-1000)** - Extract value from weaker Kings, pairs, or Queens\n3. **Large bet/All-in** - Maximum pressure, but risks losing big if trapped\n\nReason:\n\nI should make a moderate value bet. My three Kings is strong enough to bet for value, but the opponent's passive play and check on the river when the board paired Kings is concerning. A moderate bet of around 800-1200 allows me to:\n- Extract value from weaker hands (worse Kings, two pairs, Queens)\n- Not commit too much if opponent has me beaten with a full house\n- Give opponent a chance to make a crying call with a weaker hand\n\nI'll bet 1000 chips as a solid value bet that can get called by worse hands while not overcommitting if I'm beaten.\n\nAnswer: 1000"}
